.TH FASTAPI\-NEW "1" "December 2025" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
.B fastapi\-new
\(en Create a new FastAPI project in one command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fastapi\-new
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PROJECT_NAME ]
.P
If
.BR fastapi (1)
is installed:
.P
.B fastapi\ new
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PROJECT_NAME ]
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS"
.TP
.B PROJECT_NAME
The name of the new FastAPI project.
If not provided, initializes in the current directory.
.SS "OPTIONAL ARGUMENTS"
.TP
.B \-p\fR,\ \fB\-\-python\fR\ \fITEXT
Specify the Python version for the new project (e.g.,
.BR 3.14 ).
Must be
.B 3.10
or higher.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-completion
Install completion for the current shell.
.IP
Only for
.BR fastapi\-new ;
unavailable when called as
.BR fastapi\ new .
.TP
.B \-\-show\-completion
Show completion for the current shell,
to copy it or customize the installation.
.IP
Only for
.BR fastapi\-new ;
unavailable when called as
.BR fastapi\ new .
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR fastapi (1)
